✅ Top Factors That Improve Your Chances of Getting Placed at Amazon (SDE Role)
1. Strong DSA (Data Structures & Algorithms) Skills
Amazon heavily focuses on problem-solving and coding skills during interviews.

Candidates who consistently solve medium to hard LeetCode problems and participate in competitive programming stand out.

2. Deep Understanding of System Design
For experienced candidates (1.5+ years), Low-Level and High-Level Design knowledge is critical.

Understanding scalability, caching, database design, and microservices architecture adds great value.

3. Hands-on Development Experience
Having real-world projects in technologies like Java, Python, React, Node.js, AWS, etc.

Open-source contributions or personal GitHub portfolios boost credibility.

4. Alignment with Amazon’s 16 Leadership Principles
Amazon puts strong emphasis on behavioral interviews using STAR format (Situation, Task, Action, Result).

Candidates who demonstrate ownership, customer obsession, and bias for action are preferred.

5. Strong Academic/Problem-Solving Background
Students from Tier 1 engineering colleges (IITs, NITs, IIITs, BITS) may get more interview calls, but anyone with strong DSA + projects can break in.

6. Consistent Practice and Mock Interviews
Mock interviews on platforms like Pramp, Interviewing.io, or with peers help a lot.

Practicing under real-time constraints improves confidence and performance.

